US-007 is implemented and the bead is closed, but I did not run the browser check. I also did not run the e2e suite.

- **Shared filter module:** I added `frontend/src/utils/listFilter.ts`. It holds the geo-tag and the year range together and builds the single list request. When both are set, the request carries the geo-tag and the time range.
- **List loading:** `HomePage._fetchFeed` and `_buildParams` now read that request instead of reading the two filters separately.
- **Atlas state kept on a timeline change:** `ViewContext.update` used to drop the `atlas` and `view` params when only the time range changed. Picking a time range would have closed the map. It now keeps them. The page still resets to 1.
- **Tests:** `frontend/test/listFilter.test.ts` covers each filter alone, both together, and clearing each one.
- **Checks:** `scripts/check.sh --short` passes. That profile skips e2e.
- **Not done:** the playwright-cli check at 390×844 and 820×1180 is still open, and so is the PR to `atlas-sheet`.

